%description:

A deviation of Tr38901PathLossModel from the specification, pinned and not
endorsed: the outdoor-to-indoor building penetration loss of a UMa or UMi cell
below 6 GHz is the single-frequency model's in a simulation with several carrier
frequencies too.

TR 38.901 v16.1.0 7.4.3.1: "For backwards compatibility with TR 36.873 [3], the
following building penetration model should be used for UMa and UMi
single-frequency simulations at frequencies below 6 GHz.", followed by "Table
7.4.3-3. O2I building penetration loss model for single-frequency simulations
<6 GHz": PL_tw "20 dB", PL_in "0.5 d2D-in", sigma_P "0 dB". For every other
simulation Table 7.4.3-2 gives the low-loss and the high-loss model ("Both
low-loss and high-loss models are applicable to UMa and UMi-Street Canyon").

The model decides by the carrier frequency of the link and the scenario of its
cell alone; it does not know how many carrier frequencies the simulation has.

Checked in a network with two carriers, 2 GHz and 3.5 GHz, on an indoor UMa UE's
downlink at 3.5 GHz, 10 m inside its building: the O2I loss is 20 + 0.5 * 10 =
25 dB, whatever the UE's penetration deviate (sigma_P = 0) and whichever of the
two models of Table 7.4.3-2 the channel model is set to.
ChannelModelPenetrationMultiCarrierSpec asserts the specification as an expected
failure. When the model follows it, change this test together with that one.

%includes:
#include "SchedulerTestUtil.h"
#include "ChannelModelTestUtil.h"

%global:
using namespace simu5g;
using namespace simu5g::unittest;
using inet::Coord;

%file: harness.ned
import simu5g.common.binder.Binder;
import simu5g.stack.phy.medium.CellularRadioMedium;
import simu5g.common.carrierAggregation.CarrierAggregation;
import simu5g.stack.phy.channelmodel.Tr38901ChannelModel;

network Harness
{
    submodules:
        binder: Binder;
        radioMedium: CellularRadioMedium;
        carrierAggregation: CarrierAggregation;
        lowLossModel: Tr38901ChannelModel;
        highLossModel: Tr38901ChannelModel;
        test: Test;
}

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
network = Harness
cmdenv-express-mode = false
cmdenv-log-prefix = ""
sim-time-limit = 1s

# two carriers: not a single-frequency simulation
*.carrierAggregation.numComponentCarriers = 2
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].carrierFrequency = 2GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].numBands = 10
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[1].carrierFrequency = 3.5GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[1].numBands = 10
*.*Model.componentCarrierModule = "carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[1]"
**.cellInfoModule = ""
*.binder.printTrafficGeneratorConfig = false

# the path loss alone, on a LOS link
**.dynamicLos = false
**.fixedLos = true
**.shadowing = false
**.fading = false
*.highLossModel.useBuildingPenetrationHighLossModel = true
**.useBuildingPenetrationHighLossModel = false

%no-default-inifile: 1

%activity:
Checker c;
auto *lowLoss = harnessModule<StochasticChannelModel>(this, "lowLossModel");
auto *highLoss = harnessModule<StochasticChannelModel>(this, "highLossModel");

StubEndpoint bsEndpoint, ueEndpoint;
const MacNodeId bsId = MacNodeId(1);
const MacNodeId ueId = MacNodeId(1025);
bsEndpoint.nodeId = bsId;
ueEndpoint.nodeId = ueId;
bsEndpoint.coord = Coord(0, 0, 25);
ueEndpoint.coord = Coord(100, 0, 1.5);
auto *medium = harnessModule<CellularRadioMedium>(this, "radioMedium");
StubRadioRegistration bsRadio(medium, bsId, &bsEndpoint);
StubRadioRegistration ueRadio(medium, ueId, &ueEndpoint);
ChannelModelProbe lowProbe(lowLoss), highProbe(highLoss);

wait(0.010);

// the O2I loss of the UE's downlink, on the 3.5 GHz carrier: its attenuation
// indoors, 10 m from the wall, over its attenuation outdoors at the same place
RadioLink lowLink = lowProbe.whatIfLink(&ueEndpoint, dlCqiTransmission(&bsEndpoint, ueId));
RadioLink highLink = highProbe.whatIfLink(&ueEndpoint, dlCqiTransmission(&bsEndpoint, ueId));
auto o2iLoss = [&] (StochasticChannelModel *model, const RadioLink& link, double deviate) {
    ueEndpoint.insideBuilding = false;
    double outdoors = model->getAttenuation(link);
    ueEndpoint.insideBuilding = true;
    ueEndpoint.insideDistance = 10.0;
    ueEndpoint.penetrationLossDeviate = deviate;
    return model->getAttenuation(link) - outdoors;
};

c.expectNear("PINNED DEFECT: with two carriers, an indoor UMa UE's O2I loss at 3.5 GHz is the single-frequency model's 20 + 0.5 d2D-in", o2iLoss(lowLoss, lowLink, 0.0), 25.0, 1e-9);
c.expectNear("PINNED DEFECT: ...with no random term (sigma_P = 0)", o2iLoss(lowLoss, lowLink, 1.0), 25.0, 1e-9);
c.expectNear("PINNED DEFECT: ...and the same where the channel model is set to the high-loss model", o2iLoss(highLoss, highLink, 0.0), 25.0, 1e-9);
c.expectNear("PINNED DEFECT: ...with no random term either", o2iLoss(highLoss, highLink, 1.0), 25.0, 1e-9);

c.summary();

%contains: stdout
modelchecks=4 modelfailures=0

%not-contains: stdout
FAILED
